#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marker families, the ordered run scanner, the Prettier-compatible [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renumber engine, and the single-TextEdit list-edit planner; refactor the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hyphen helpers onto the shared primitives with no behavior change.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]INSERT-mode Ctrl+J for ordered items[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]newline[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]newline: route Ctrl+J through the list-edit planner so ordered items [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]continue, split, grow a first sibling, exit from an empty marker, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]de-list at the content column, each as one undo checkpoint with the run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renumbered.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]NORMAL-mode o and O for ordered items[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]openline[dim] · [dim][/dim]after newline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]openline: add an optional planned-edit hook to the vim open-line [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commands so prompt panes open a correctly numbered ordered sibling below[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or above, renumber the run, and keep dot-repeat recomputing at the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]destination.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]INSERT-mode Tab and Shift+Tab nesting for ordered items[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]shift[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shift: make Tab nest an ordered item under its parent at that parent's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]content column (starting a nested list at 1) and Shift+Tab unnest it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into the enclosing run, renumbering both the source and destination runs[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and moving the item's owned block with it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]NORMAL-mode J for ordered items[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]join[dim] · [dim][/dim]after openline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]join: drop a pulled-up ordered marker when folding the next line up, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]renumber the run the removed item left behind.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ordered-marker highlighting[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]highlight[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlight: give ordered markers the same theme-aware accent the leading [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bullet dash already gets, with unit coverage and a PNG snapshot fixture.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, help modal, and full verification[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after newline, openline, shift, join, highlight[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: document the ordered-list behavior in the ace reference and help [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal, and run the exhaustive verification lane over the combined tree.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-gi","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-gi.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-47845b18a62b655df1ab0e928935b89a","started_at":"2026-08-06T19:25:21.546396+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"6ba7064c8911813c15a17d3f4be9ef5bfc14401bc836835647a4498f5